# openapi-typescript@^7.13.0's own peerDependencies still say
# `typescript@^5.x` — stale relative to this project's `~6.0.2` pin, not a
# real incompatibility (both have worked together throughout this branch's
# own `tsc -b`/`vite build` runs). A plain local `npm install` silently
# accepts a peer mismatch like this (warns, doesn't fail); `npm ci` — what
# `backend/Dockerfile`'s frontend-build stage actually runs — treats it as
# a hard ERESOLVE error instead. Discovered running a real
# `docker compose up -d --build` for the first time since Phase 2.1
# (REBUILD_STATUS.md's own tracked Open Question), not something Phase 3.4
# introduced. legacy-peer-deps here is what makes `npm ci` behave like the
# `npm install` every local build has already been implicitly relying on.
legacy-peer-deps=true
